{"content":[{"c":["ELIADA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of King David’s sons, born in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.5.16","r":"2Sam.5.16","rawR":"2Sam.5.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.5.16","value":"2Sam.5.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 5:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.8","r":"1Chr.3.8","rawR":"1Chr.3.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.8","value":"1Chr.3.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:8"},"). He is also called Beeliada in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.14.7","r":"1Chr.14.7","rawR":"1Chr.14.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.14.7","value":"1Chr.14.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 14:7"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Father of Rezon, the king of Damascus and an adversary of Solomon (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.11.23","r":"1Kgs.11.23","rawR":"1Kgs.11.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.11.23","value":"1Kgs.11.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 11:23"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. General under King Jehoshaphat. Eliada and the 200,000 warriors he commanded were from Benjamin’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.17.17","r":"2Chr.17.17","rawR":"2Chr.17.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.17.17","value":"2Chr.17.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 17:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Eliada","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 5:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.5.16","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.5.16","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.5.16"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.8","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.8","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.8"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 14:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.14.7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.14.7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.14.7"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 11:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_works